# GROMACS 2025.3 – Molecular Dynamics Simulation

## Description

GROMACS is a molecular dynamics simulation package used to investigate the structural stability and dynamic behavior of biomolecular systems.

GROMACS 2025.3 was used to perform a 100 ns molecular dynamics simulation of the vaccine–TLR4 complex.

## 1. Installation and Version Check

```bash
gmx --version
```

Confirm that the installed version is GROMACS 2025.3.

## 2. Input Preparation

Prepare the docked protein complex in PDB format.

```bash
mkdir -p GROMACS_Project/{Input,Simulation,Analysis}
```

Place the structure in:

```text
GROMACS_Project/
├── Input/
│   └── complex.pdb
├── Simulation/
└── Analysis/
```

## 3. Generate Protein Topology

```bash
cd GROMACS_Project/Simulation

gmx pdb2gmx \
-f ../Input/complex.pdb \
-o processed.gro \
-p topol.top \
-ff gromos54a7 \
-water tip3p
```

Select the appropriate protonation states and termini when prompted. The selected water model must be supported by the installed force-field files.

## 4. Define the Simulation Box

A cubic box with a minimum solute-to-edge distance of 15 Å:

```bash
gmx editconf \
-f processed.gro \
-o boxed.gro \
-c \
-d 1.5 \
-bt cubic
```

## 5. Solvate the System

Use a solvent coordinate file compatible with the selected water model.

```bash
gmx solvate \
-cp boxed.gro \
-cs spc216.gro \
-o solvated.gro \
-p topol.top
```

## 6. Energy Minimization Parameter File

Create:

```bash
nano em.mdp
```

```ini
integrator      = steep
emtol           = 1000.0
emstep          = 0.01
nsteps          = 5000

cutoff-scheme   = Verlet
nstlist         = 10
rlist           = 0.9

coulombtype     = PME
rcoulomb        = 0.9

vdwtype         = Cut-off
rvdw            = 0.9

pbc             = xyz
```

## 7. Add Ions

Generate the input file:

```bash
gmx grompp \
-f em.mdp \
-c solvated.gro \
-p topol.top \
-o ions.tpr
```

Add 0.15 M NaCl and neutralize the system:

```bash
gmx genion \
-s ions.tpr \
-o solv_ions.gro \
-p topol.top \
-pname NA \
-nname CL \
-conc 0.15 \
-neutral
```

Select the `SOL` group when prompted.

## 8. Energy Minimization

```bash
gmx grompp \
-f em.mdp \
-c solv_ions.gro \
-p topol.top \
-o em.tpr

gmx mdrun -deffnm em
```

Extract potential energy:

```bash
gmx energy \
-f em.edr \
-o potential_energy.xvg
```

Select `Potential` when prompted.

## 9. NVT Equilibration

Create:

```bash
nano nvt.mdp
```

```ini
define                  = -DPOSRES
integrator              = md
dt                      = 0.002
nsteps                  = 50000

nstxout-compressed      = 500
nstenergy               = 500
nstlog                  = 500

cutoff-scheme           = Verlet
nstlist                 = 20
rlist                   = 0.9

coulombtype             = PME
rcoulomb                = 0.9

vdwtype                 = Cut-off
rvdw                    = 0.9

tcoupl                  = V-rescale
tc-grps                 = System
tau-t                   = 1.0
ref-t                   = 300

pcoupl                  = no

constraints             = h-bonds
constraint-algorithm    = lincs

pbc                     = xyz

gen-vel                 = yes
gen-temp                = 300
gen-seed                = -1
```

Generate and run:

```bash
gmx grompp \
-f nvt.mdp \
-c em.gro \
-r em.gro \
-p topol.top \
-o nvt.tpr

gmx mdrun -deffnm nvt
```

Extract temperature:

```bash
gmx energy \
-f nvt.edr \
-o temperature.xvg
```

Select `Temperature` when prompted.

## 10. NPT Equilibration

Create:

```bash
nano npt.mdp
```

```ini
define                  = -DPOSRES
integrator              = md
dt                      = 0.002
nsteps                  = 50000

nstxout-compressed      = 500
nstenergy               = 500
nstlog                  = 500

cutoff-scheme           = Verlet
nstlist                 = 20
rlist                   = 0.9

coulombtype             = PME
rcoulomb                = 0.9

vdwtype                 = Cut-off
rvdw                    = 0.9

tcoupl                  = V-rescale
tc-grps                 = System
tau-t                   = 1.0
ref-t                   = 300

pcoupl                  = C-rescale
pcoupltype              = isotropic
tau-p                   = 5.0
ref-p                   = 1.0
compressibility         = 4.5e-5

constraints             = h-bonds
constraint-algorithm    = lincs

refcoord-scaling        = com

pbc                     = xyz

continuation            = yes
gen-vel                 = no
```

Generate and run:

```bash
gmx grompp \
-f npt.mdp \
-c nvt.gro \
-r nvt.gro \
-t nvt.cpt \
-p topol.top \
-o npt.tpr

gmx mdrun -deffnm npt
```

Extract pressure:

```bash
gmx energy \
-f npt.edr \
-o pressure.xvg
```

Extract density:

```bash
gmx energy \
-f npt.edr \
-o density.xvg
```

Select the corresponding energy terms when prompted.

## 11. Production Molecular Dynamics Simulation

Create:

```bash
nano md.mdp
```

```ini
integrator              = md
dt                      = 0.002
nsteps                  = 50000000

nstxout-compressed      = 500
nstenergy               = 5000
nstlog                  = 5000

cutoff-scheme           = Verlet
nstlist                 = 20
rlist                   = 0.9

coulombtype             = PME
rcoulomb                = 0.9

vdwtype                 = Cut-off
rvdw                    = 0.9

tcoupl                  = V-rescale
tc-grps                 = System
tau-t                   = 1.0
ref-t                   = 300

pcoupl                  = C-rescale
pcoupltype              = isotropic
tau-p                   = 5.0
ref-p                   = 1.0
compressibility         = 4.5e-5

constraints             = h-bonds
constraint-algorithm    = lincs
lincs-iter              = 1
lincs-order             = 4

pbc                     = xyz

continuation            = yes
gen-vel                 = no
```

Generate the production input:

```bash
gmx grompp \
-f md.mdp \
-c npt.gro \
-t npt.cpt \
-p topol.top \
-o md.tpr
```

Run the 100 ns simulation:

```bash
gmx mdrun \
-deffnm md \
-ntmpi 1 \
-ntomp 8
```

The simulation uses a 2 fs timestep:

```text
100 ns = 100,000 ps

100,000 / 0.002 = 50,000,000 steps
```

## 12. Trajectory Analysis

### 12.1. RMSD

```bash
gmx rms \
-s md.tpr \
-f md.xtc \
-o rmsd.xvg \
-tu ns
```

Select the appropriate fitting and calculation groups.

### 12.2. RMSF

```bash
gmx rmsf \
-s md.tpr \
-f md.xtc \
-o rmsf.xvg \
-res
```

Select the C-alpha or Backbone group.

### 12.3. Radius of Gyration

```bash
gmx gyrate \
-s md.tpr \
-f md.xtc \
-o gyrate.xvg
```

### 12.4. Hydrogen Bond Analysis

```bash
gmx hbond \
-s md.tpr \
-f md.xtc \
-num hydrogen_bonds.xvg
```

Select the appropriate groups for the intended analysis.

### 12.5. Trajectory Check

```bash
gmx check -f md.xtc
```

## 13. Output Files

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| `topol.top` | System topology |
| `processed.gro` | Processed protein structure |
| `em.gro` | Energy-minimized structure |
| `nvt.gro` | NVT-equilibrated structure |
| `npt.gro` | NPT-equilibrated structure |
| `md.xtc` | Production trajectory |
| `md.edr` | Energy data |
| `md.log` | Simulation log |
| `rmsd.xvg` | RMSD data |
| `rmsf.xvg` | RMSF data |
| `gyrate.xvg` | Radius of gyration data |
| `hydrogen_bonds.xvg` | Hydrogen-bond data |

